-- title:
--   The observable projection satisfies a polynomial Poincaré inequality
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, $I=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, $E=I\times\{0,1\}$, and $\Omega=\mathcal P(E)$. Let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean oracles on subsets of $I$. Write $R(S)$ for the natural-number value of the paired-rank routine with parameter $r$ and these oracles, and $d(S)=n-R(S)$ with subtraction truncated at zero. Let $M_1,M_2$ be matroids with ground set $I$ and common rank $r$, and assume $o_j$ returns true exactly on independent sets of $M_j$, for $j=1,2$. A transversal selects one label from each pair; let $T$ be this class. For distinct $i,k\in I$, let $D_{ik}$ be the class having pair $i$ empty, pair $k$ full, and every other pair singly occupied. All other states are invalid. For $q>0$ and positive rational multipliers $w_{ik}$, define $C(q)=\sum_{S\in T}q^{d(S)}$, $D_{ik}(q)=\sum_{S\in D_{ik}}q^{d(S)}$, and $\lambda(S)=q^{d(S)}$ on $T$, $\lambda(S)=w_{ik}q^{d(S)}$ on $D_{ik}$, and $\lambda(S)=0$ on invalid states. Let $Z_w=\sum_S\lambda(S)$ and $\pi(S)=\lambda(S)/Z_w$. For $n>0$, let $Q(S,U)$ be the probability that swapping two independently uniform labels of $E$ sends $S$ to $U$. Let $P$ be its Metropolis kernel with target $\pi$, and set $\kappa(S,U)=Q(S,U)\min(\pi(S),\pi(U))$. Write $\mathcal E_\kappa(H)=\frac12\sum_{S,U}\kappa(S,U)(H(S)-H(U))^2$. Assume $0<q\le1$ and $\frac14 C(q)/D_{ik}(q)\le w_{ik}\le4C(q)/D_{ik}(q)$ for every distinct $i,k$. For a state function $H:\Omega\to\mathbb R$, let $\Pi H$ agree with $H$ on transversals, equal the $\pi$-conditional mean of $H$ on each defect class, and be zero on invalid states. A conditional mean on a zero-mass class is defined to be zero. Use $\langle f,g\rangle_\pi=\sum_S\pi(S)f(S)g(S)$, $\mathbb E_\pi f=\sum_S\pi(S)f(S)$, and $\operatorname{Var}_\pi f=\mathbb E_\pi[(f-\mathbb E_\pi f)^2]$. Then every $H:\Omega\to\mathbb R$ satisfies $$\operatorname{Var}_\pi(\Pi H)\le2000n^6\,\mathcal D_{\pi,P}(H),\qquad \mathcal D_{\pi,P}(H)=\frac12\sum_{S,U}\pi(S)P(S,U)(H(S)-H(U))^2.$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ObservablePoincare.lean#L94-L251

